From: Oever Gonzalez <software@notengobattery.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt76: expose the tx token pool in debugfs

Token exhaustion is invisible from userspace: when the pool runs dry the
driver simply stops accepting frames, and every symptom appears
somewhere else. On airoha NPU offload, the NPU's handoff queue reporting
full forever -- wireless side apparently idle, kernel silent -- looks
exactly like it, and there is no way to tell the two apart without
rebuilding the driver. These counters are what ruled it out there: 2-26
tokens in flight throughout a wedge that turned out to be a ring
handshake fault.

Print the counters the allocator already maintains, so a leak can be
watched as it develops rather than inferred after the fact.

Report token_start with them. The counters cover the ids the driver
allocates, which start above whatever an offload engine has reserved;
on airoha NPU that leaves the entire 8192-entry hardware pool -- the one
the offload path actually draws from -- outside the numbers printed
here. Without the start id the file reads as if it covered everything.

--- a/debugfs.c
+++ b/debugfs.c
@@ -88,6 +88,27 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static int mt76_tokens_read(struct seq_file *s, void *data)
+{
+	struct mt76_dev *dev = dev_get_drvdata(s->private);
+	u16 count, wed_count;
+
+	spin_lock_bh(&dev->token_lock);
+	count = dev->token_count;
+	wed_count = dev->wed_token_count;
+	spin_unlock_bh(&dev->token_lock);
+
+	seq_printf(s, "token_count %u\n", count);
+	seq_printf(s, "wed_token_count %u\n", wed_count);
+	seq_printf(s, "token_size %u\n", dev->token_size);
+	/* ids below token_start belong to an offload engine and are not
+	 * accounted here: on airoha NPU that is the whole hardware pool
+	 */
+	seq_printf(s, "token_start %u\n", dev->token_start);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
 void mt76_seq_puts_array(struct seq_file *file, const char *str,
 			 s8 *val, int len)
 {
@@ -120,6 +141,8 @@
 		debugfs_create_blob("otp", 0400, dir, &dev->otp);
 	debugfs_create_devm_seqfile(dev->dev, "rx-queues", dir,
 				    mt76_rx_queues_read);
+	debugfs_create_devm_seqfile(dev->dev, "tokens", dir,
+				    mt76_tokens_read);
 
 	return dir;
 }
